{{- define "content" }}
{{- $codes := index . "areaCodeEntries" }}
{{- $regions := index . "regionEntries" }}
{{- $abbrs := index . "abbrEntries" }}
{{- $placeholder := "Lookup area codes, states, or abbreviations (e.g. CA, 201, Texas)" }}
{{/*delay:150ms is probably the lowest value, as anything lower and the changes can be skipped*/}}
<div class="container-xxl">
<div class="bg-body-tertiary border rounded p-3 mb-4">
  <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-2 mb-3">
    <div class="input-group input-group-sm" style="max-width: 34rem;">
      <span class="input-group-text">
        <span id="areacodes-indicator" class="htmx-indicator spinner-border spinner-border-sm text-secondary" role="status">
          <span class="visually-hidden">Searching...</span>
        </span>
      </span>
      <input type="search" class="form-control" name="htmx-search"
        id="areacodes-search"
        placeholder="{{$placeholder}}"
        aria-label="{{$placeholder}}"
        autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
        hx-trigger="input changed delay:150ms, search"
        hx-post="/areacodes"
        hx-target="#areacodes-results"
        hx-indicator="#areacodes-indicator" autofocus>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" id="areacodes-clear" disabled>Clear</button>
    </div>
    <span class="small text-body-secondary">Comma-separate multiple lookups</span>
  </div>
  <nav class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-1 pt-2 border-top" aria-label="Area code sections">
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary py-0 px-2" href="#sec-codes">By area code{{if $codes}} ({{len $codes}}){{end}}</a>
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary py-0 px-2" href="#sec-regions">By state &amp; province{{if $regions}} ({{len $regions}}){{end}}</a>
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary py-0 px-2" href="#sec-abbr">By 2-letter code{{if $abbrs}} ({{len $abbrs}}){{end}}</a>
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary py-0 px-2" href="#sec-about">About</a>
    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary py-0 px-2" href="#sec-sources">Data sources</a>
  </nav>
</div>

<div id="areacodes-results"></div>

<section id="sec-codes" class="mb-5" style="scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem;">
  <h2 class="h4 border-bottom pb-2 mb-3 d-flex align-items-baseline justify-content-between">
    <span>By area code</span>
    {{- if $codes}}<span class="small fw-normal text-body-secondary">{{len $codes}} codes</span>{{end}}
  </h2>
  <div style="column-width: 24rem; column-gap: 0.75rem;">
  {{- range $codes }}
    <div class="pb-2" style="break-inside: avoid;">
      <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3 p-2 px-3 rounded border bg-body-tertiary">
        <span class="font-monospace fw-bold fs-5 text-primary-emphasis bg-primary-subtle border border-primary-subtle rounded px-2 py-1 lh-1 flex-shrink-0">{{.Code}}</span>
        <div>
          <div class="fw-medium">{{.Regions}}</div>
          {{- if ne .Note "" }}
          <div class="small text-body-secondary mt-1">{{.Note}}</div>
          {{- end }}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {{- end }}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="sec-regions" class="mb-5" style="scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem;">
  <h2 class="h4 border-bottom pb-2 mb-3 d-flex align-items-baseline justify-content-between">
    <span>By state, province, or territory</span>
    {{- if $regions}}<span class="small fw-normal text-body-secondary">{{len $regions}} regions</span>{{end}}
  </h2>
  <div style="column-width: 22rem; column-gap: 0.75rem;">
  {{- range $regions }}
    <div class="pb-2" style="break-inside: avoid;">
      <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start gap-2 p-2 px-3 rounded border bg-body-tertiary">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
          {{- if ne .Abbr "" }}
          <span class="small font-monospace fw-semibold text-primary-emphasis bg-primary-subtle border border-primary-subtle rounded px-2 py-1 lh-1 flex-shrink-0">{{.Abbr}}</span>
          {{- end }}
          <span class="fw-medium text-nowrap">{{.Name}}</span>
        </div>
        <span class="font-monospace small text-body-secondary text-end">{{.Codes}}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  {{- end }}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="sec-abbr" class="mb-5" style="scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem;">
  <h2 class="h4 border-bottom pb-2 mb-3 d-flex align-items-baseline justify-content-between">
    <span>By 2-letter abbreviations</span>
    {{- if $abbrs}}<span class="small fw-normal text-body-secondary">{{len $abbrs}} codes</span>{{end}}
  </h2>
  <div style="column-width: 18rem; column-gap: 0.75rem;">
  {{- range $abbrs }}
    <div class="pb-2" style="break-inside: avoid;">
      <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3 p-2 px-3 rounded border bg-body-tertiary">
        <span class="font-monospace fw-bold fs-5 text-primary-emphasis bg-primary-subtle border border-primary-subtle rounded px-2 py-1 lh-1 flex-shrink-0">{{.Abbr}}</span>
        <div>
          <div class="fw-medium">{{.Name}}</div>
          <div class="font-monospace small text-body-secondary">{{.Codes}}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {{- end }}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="sec-about" class="mb-4" style="scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem;">
  <h2 class="h4 border-bottom pb-2 mb-3">About</h2>
  <p class="mb-0">
    The telephone numbering plan of 1994 uses a 3-digit area code and a 7-digit telephone number within the United States, Canada, the Caribbean and the U.S. territories.
    Using the format of <em>2xx ... 8xx, 9xx</em>, whereby <u>xx</u> could only be <em>01-19</em>, ie 201-219, 301-319, etc.
    Some sequences were reserved, such as <em>x11</em>, ie 411 and 911.
    <br>
    This page lists the area codes that were in use during the BBS era from the 1970s until the end of 1994. 
    1995 and the following years saw the introduction of new area codes formats and overlay sharing, but they are not covered here.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="sec-sources" class="mb-3" style="scroll-margin-top: 4.5rem;">
  <h2 class="h4 border-bottom pb-2 mb-3">Data sources</h2>
  <ul class="list-unstyled mb-2">
    <li>The initial area code data was sourced from the 1990, <a href="https://defacto2.net/f/ac1cb6a">NAP/PA Area Code Listing</a> which was somewhat incomplete.</li>
    <li>The data was then cross-referenced with a 1991 MS-DOS application titled Find Area Code v1.0 (c) 1991 by MPM Enterprises.</li>
    <li>Complicated data for California was sourced from the <a href="https://www.cpuc.ca.gov/industries-and-topics/internet-and-phone/area-codes-and-numbering">CA Public Utilities Commission</a>.</li>
    <li>Finally the gaps between 1990 and 1994 were filled with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_North_American_Numbering_Plan_area_codes">Wikipedia data</a>.</li>
    <li>Also old articles <small>(<a href="https://www.nytimes.com/1984/12/29/nyregion/shift-from-212-to-718-code-pains-3-boroughs.html">1984</a>, <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/1991/06/02/nyregion/201-609-and-now-oh-my-908.html">1991</a>)</small> in the New York Times helped confirm some dates.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-0">
    If you're after other international dialing codes the <a href="https://www.itu.int/oth/T0202.aspx?parent=T0202">International Telecommunication Union has a complete list</a>.
  </p>
</section>
</div>

<script>
(() => {
  const input = document.getElementById('areacodes-search');
  const clearBtn = document.getElementById('areacodes-clear');
  const results = document.getElementById('areacodes-results');
  if (!input || !clearBtn || !results) return;

  function syncClear() {
    clearBtn.disabled = input.value === '';
  }
  function resetSearch() {
    input.value = '';
    results.innerHTML = '';
    syncClear();
    input.focus();
  }

  input.addEventListener('input', syncClear);
  input.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && input.value !== '') {
      e.preventDefault();
      resetSearch();
    }
  });
  clearBtn.addEventListener('click', resetSearch);
  window.addEventListener('pageshow', syncClear);
  syncClear();
})();
</script>
{{- end}}
